From: Andrei Gosman <andrei.gosman@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 08 Sep 2026 10:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 001] fix: getaddrinfo rejects SOCK_STREAM with IPPROTO_SCTP on Darwin

Darwin has no kernel SCTP, and its getaddrinfo() refuses the hint pair
SOCK_STREAM plus IPPROTO_SCTP with EAI_BADHINTS. This holds for every host
and every address family, verified for "::", "0.0.0.0" and "127.0.0.1"
under AF_UNSPEC and AF_INET alike, while the same call with protocol 0 or
IPPROTO_TCP succeeds.

addrinfo_helper() passes the caller's protocol straight into the hints, so
on Darwin every SCTP server failed before it reached bind(). In osmo-stp
this appeared as "Unable to bind xUA server to IP(s)" with the M3UA
listener never coming up.

Only the name and the port need resolving here, and the caller reads the
protocol back out of the results to create the socket. Ask for an
unspecified protocol and restore IPPROTO_SCTP in the returned list, which
is the shape the file already uses to work around the glibc SOCK_RAW and
IPPROTO_GRE problem a few lines above.
---
diff --git a/src/core/socket.c b/src/core/socket.c
index 3a2d7b75..a9fb86c7 100644
--- a/src/core/socket.c
+++ b/src/core/socket.c
@@ -84,6 +84,17 @@ static struct addrinfo *addrinfo_helper(uint16_t family, uint16_t type, uint8_t
 	if (passive)
 		hints.ai_flags |= AI_PASSIVE;
 
+#ifdef __APPLE__
+	/* Darwin has no kernel SCTP, and its getaddrinfo() rejects the pair
+	 * SOCK_STREAM plus IPPROTO_SCTP with EAI_BADHINTS for every host and
+	 * family. Only the name and the port need resolving here, so ask for
+	 * an unspecified protocol and put IPPROTO_SCTP back into the results
+	 * below. This mirrors the SOCK_RAW workaround above. */
+	bool darwin_sctp_hint = (hints.ai_protocol == IPPROTO_SCTP);
+	if (darwin_sctp_hint)
+		hints.ai_protocol = 0;
+#endif
+
 	rc = getaddrinfo(host, portbuf, &hints, &result);
 	if (rc != 0) {
 		LOGP(DLGLOBAL, LOGL_ERROR, "getaddrinfo(%s, %u) failed: %s\n",
@@ -97,6 +108,10 @@ static struct addrinfo *addrinfo_helper(uint16_t family, uint16_t type, uint8_t
 			rp->ai_socktype = SOCK_RAW;
 			rp->ai_protocol = proto;
 		}
+#ifdef __APPLE__
+		if (darwin_sctp_hint)
+			rp->ai_protocol = IPPROTO_SCTP;
+#endif
 	}
 
 	return result;
